# GetClientele — HTTPie examples (save as `scripts/httpie/test_api.http`)

### 1) Login (get access token)
POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login/ Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "password"
}

# Save token in a shell variable (bash):
# export TOKEN=$(http --body POST http://localhost:8000/auth/login/ username=admin password=password | jq -r .access)

### 2) List vendors (no auth required)
GET http://localhost:8000/vendors/

### 3) Create a vendor (authenticated)
POST http://localhost:8000/vendors/ Authorization:"Bearer {{TOKEN}}" Content-Type: application/json

{
  "business_name": "Tasty Tacos",
  "is_mobile": true,
  "location": {"lat": -1.0, "lng": 36.8}
}

### 4) Call AI similar products
POST http://localhost:8000/api/ai/similar/ Content-Type: application/json

{
  "products": [
    {"id": 1, "name": "Chai", "description": "tea"},
    {"id": 2, "name": "Coffee", "description": "hot"}
  ],
  "product_id": 1,
  "top_k": 3
}

# Tips:
# - Use `http --session=dev` to persist cookies or session headers across requests.
# - Replace `{{TOKEN}}` with the actual token value obtained from the login response.
# - The snippet above assumes a local dev server at http://localhost:8000
